[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Aliasing note (not a rejection, but an unchecked precondition)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `src` is `const float *` and `dest` is `float *`; the C declares no `restrict`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and performs no overlap check. At `-O0` gcc reads all three `src` elements into
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m stack slots *before* any store to `dest`, so full or partial aliasing
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`dest == src`, `dest == src+1`, `dest == src-1`, …) is well-defined in practice.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The Rust reads `h`, `s`, `l` into locals up front for the same reason. Covered by
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `CONFIGS.md` rows 27–29 rather than here, since no error is produced.
